This software adapts scientific algorithms and numerical control flow from:

DEXSeq 1.58.0 (GPL >= 3)
Original authors: Simon Anders and Alejandro Reyes.
Maintainer in the inspected release: Hugo Gruson.
https://bioconductor.org/packages/DEXSeq

DESeq2 1.52.0 (LGPL >= 3)
Original principal authors: Michael I. Love, Wolfgang Huber, and Simon Anders.
The inspected C++ numerical source additionally credits Constantin Ahlmann-Eltze.
https://bioconductor.org/packages/DESeq2

Changes: rewritten in Python/NumPy/SciPy with explicit pandas table contracts,
two-condition model construction, an unpenalized damped-Newton GLM optimizer,
restricted mean-trend dispersion support, and explicit unsupported-boundary
statuses. Normalization and dispersion routines retain upstream algorithmic
structure. No claim of clean-room development or author endorsement is made.

The adapted DESeq2 material is conveyed under GPL-3.0-or-later using the option
in LGPLv3 section 3. The original LGPL license text is retained in
LICENSES/LGPL-3.0.txt, and the complete GPLv3 text is in LICENSE.

See PROVENANCE.md and reference/source-audit.json for exact source revisions,
file hashes, references, and validation provenance.
